   published works, archives, package registries, or datasets.
2. Use the code, story, characters, dialogue, narration, artwork, music, sound
   design or video in any commercial product, client work, monetized channel,
   app, game, or paid course.
3. Create derivative works: remixes, re-edits, dubs, translations, sequels,
   prequels, spin-offs, character re-use, or adaptations to other media.
4. Re-upload, re-host, or re-cut the episodes, in whole or in part, including
   on YouTube, TikTok, Instagram, Facebook, X or any other platform.
5. Use the material to train, fine-tune or evaluate machine learning models, or
   to generate synthetic media derived from it.
6. Use the names, character designs or visual identity of the series in a way
   that suggests endorsement, partnership or authorship.
7. Remove or alter copyright notices, watermarks or attribution.

The episode masters (MP4 files) are deliberately not included in this
repository. They are not public domain and are not licensed by their absence.

